  "notes": "{仕立|した}てる primarily means to tailor or sew clothing, but also extends to shaping or training a person.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pattern: Xを{仕立|した}てる\n\nSENSE 1 — TAILORING:\n- {服|ふく}を{仕立|した}てる: to make clothes\n- オーダーメイドで{仕立|した}てる: to have custom-made\n- {着物|きもの}を{仕立|した}てる: to make a kimono\n\nSENSE 2 — TRAINING/SHAPING:\n- {一人前|いちにんまえ}に{仕立|した}てる: to train someone to be fully capable\n- {犯人|はんにん}に{仕立|した}てる: to frame someone as the culprit\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{仕立|した}てている means 'is in the process of making/tailoring.'\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {仕立|した}て{屋|や}: tailor (shop/person)\n- {仕立|した}て: tailoring; the way something is made",
